course: dictionary
lesson: 14267
title: Nimble: quick and light
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Nimble» describes someone or something that moves quickly, easily and lightly. «The nimble goat leapt from rock to rock.» The goat did not stumble or slow down. It jumped quickly and lightly, so nimble means quick and light on the feet.
explain: The word can also describe a quick, clever mind. «Her nimble mind solved the puzzle in seconds.» Her mind worked fast and sharply, so the puzzle was solved in seconds. You can also have nimble fingers, which are good at fine, careful work like knitting or playing the piano.
explain: To check a meaning, swap your idea into the sentence. Try «The goat leapt from rock to rock» with quick and light in place of nimble. Does it still make sense? If yes, you have found the right meaning.
fact: «Nimble» means able to move quickly, easily and lightly.
fact: «Nimble» can also mean quick and clever in thinking, as in «a nimble mind».
fact: «Nimble fingers» means good at fine work, such as knitting or playing the piano.
fact: The nursery rhyme «Jack be nimble, Jack be quick» uses the word to mean fast and light on your feet.
fact: The comparative form is «nimbler» (more nimble), and the superlative is «nimblest» (most nimble).
exercise: «The nimble goat leapt from rock to rock.» What does nimble mean? | Clumsy and slow | Very large | *Able to move quickly and lightly | Sleepy
exercise: «She has nimble fingers and can knit very fast.» What do nimble fingers mean? | Fingers that are very long | *Good at fine, careful work | Fingers that are sore | Fingers that are dirty
exercise: Which phrase describes someone who thinks quickly and cleverly? | a heavy heart | a cold nose | *a nimble mind | a sleepy head
test: «The nimble cat jumped onto the wall in one bound.» What does nimble mean here? | Lazy | Angry | Heavy | *Quick and light
test: Which word is the comparative of nimble, meaning more nimble? | nimblest | nimbly | nimbleness | *nimbler
exam: «The nimble dancer spun and leapt across the stage.» Which words in the sentence give you the clue to the meaning of nimble? | the word stage | nothing, you cannot tell | *spun and leapt | the word The
